 thing to a plan to replace  it he was asked about this report from  the Congressional Budget Office saying  24 million will lose insurance it's a  disaster he said the report is offering  an incomplete picture be  it isn't taking into account the  regulatory steps that he intends to take  as well as other legislation that  Republicans plan to pass as part of  their multi-step strategy to repeal and  replace the health care law what does  that even mean what Tom Price is  suggesting here is that Republicans are  also going to cut out regulations in  ways which we don't yet know it's a  wacky funhouse mirror we just don't know  what reality is and it's gonna  completely change the circumstances so  that 24 million people will not actually  lose coverage and I guess we'll save way  more money than the paltry 37 billion a  year he said quote we disagree  strenuously with the report that was put  out well I'm convinced folks Paul Ryan  focusing on the premiums being lower in  ten years part ignoring that premiums  would be higher for many years saying in  ten years premiums will be ten percent  lower than the currently projected  numbers which of course will be still  way higher than they are today  truth is we can't really project that  accurately ten years out and 10% lower  than expected in ten years if true it's  not even particularly impressive okay  now one's talking point that it's  important to debunk right now many  Republicans are saying well listen David  some of those millions of uninsured are  going to be uninsured by choice because  it's young people who never wanted  health insurance under Obama care anyway  they're healthy and they are now going  to be able to exercise their  individualism and freedom and not be  forced to buy insurance by a bogus  federal health care mandate that's true  some of them are healthy and they will  be fine but many won't and will end up  using the emergency room as their doctor  when they get sick many will never pay  because they'll get a huge bill and  that's all going to be priced into the  premiums that people who do have  insurance will pay and that's going to  drive premiums up and that's going to  include people who need health insurance  and can't afford to pay more who will  have to pay more because so-called  healthy young people will get sick at  least some of them there is an  alternative okay  because the real discussion shouldn't be  whether we have a a che or a CA the real  discussion should be that our entire  health care system is morally bankrupt  there's something called HR 676 the  expanded and improved Medicare for all  Act sponsored once again by congressman  john conyers a democrat from michigan  introduced on january 24th 2017 fewer  than two months ago the bill establishes  Medicare for all to include everybody in  the United States it would destroy the  for-profit health insurance market  because it says that health insurers may  not sell health insurance that  duplicates the benefits provided under  the bill insurers would only be allowed  to sell insurance for benefits that are  not medically necessary like cosmetic  surgery and the program would be funded  from existing sources of government  revenue for health care by increasing  personal income taxes on the top 5% of  income earners by instituting a  progressive excise tax on payroll and  self-employment income by instituting  attacks on unearned income and by  instituting a tax on stock and bond  transactions call your elected officials  tell them specifically I support HR 676  I will vote you out if you don't support  HR 676 you can go to who is my  representative dot-com to find out who  your representatives are call email  every single one of them
 

